# Security considerations # {#security-considerations}

# Privacy considerations # {#privacy-considerations}

# Framework # {#framework}

## Registration attempts ## {#framework-registration-attempts}

A <dfn>registration attempt</dfn> is a [=struct=] representing an in-flight or completed DBSC registration started by [=process a session registration=]. It has the following [=struct/items=]:

<dl dfn-for="registration attempt">
  : <dfn>registration URL</dfn>
  :: A [=URL=].
  : <dfn>provider URL</dfn>
  :: Null or a [=URL=], initially null.
  : <dfn>provider session ID</dfn>
  :: Null or a [=string=], initially null.
  : <dfn>end time</dfn>
  :: Null or a [=coarsened moment=] on the [=wall clock=], initially null.
  : <dfn>success</dfn>
  :: A [=boolean=], initially false.
  : <dfn>resulting session</dfn>
  :: A [=device bound session=] or null, initially null.
  : <dfn>reason</dfn>
  :: A [=string=] or null, initially null.
  : <dfn>code</dfn>
  :: Null or a [=16-bit unsigned integer=], initially null.
  : <dfn>associated document</dfn>
  :: A {{Document}} or null, initially null.
  : <dfn>completed</dfn>
  :: A [=boolean=], initially false.
</dl>

A <dfn>registration waiter</dfn> is a [=struct=] that tracks a pending `waitForRegistrations()` call and the [=registration attempts=] it waits on. It has the following [=struct/items=]:

<dl dfn-for="registration waiter">
  : <dfn>promise</dfn>
  :: A {{Promise}}.
  : <dfn>environment</dfn>
  :: An [=environment settings object=].
  : <dfn>captured attempts</dfn>
  :: A [=list=] of completed [=registration attempts=].
  : <dfn>remaining</dfn>
  :: A [=set=] of [=registration attempts=].
</dl>

## Per-document registration state ## {#document-registration-state}

A document tracks its same-origin DBSC registrations while they are in flight, buffers their outcomes once they finish.

Each {{Document}} has:

- <dfn for="Document">pending registrations</dfn>, a [=set=] of [=registration attempts=], initially empty.
- <dfn for="Document">registration buffer</dfn>, a [=list=] of completed [=registration attempts=], initially empty.
- <dfn for="Document">registration waiters</dfn>, a [=list=] of [=registration waiters=], initially empty.

User agents should cap the [=list/size=] of a {{Document}}'s [=Document/registration buffer=] at an [=implementation-defined=] limit, removing the earliest-appended entries first.

When the user agent clears cookies or site data for an [=origin=] or site (including via [:Clear-Site-Data:] [[clear-site-data]]), it must [=list/empty=] the [=Document/registration buffer=] of each {{Document}} whose [=Document/origin=] is affected.

This specification defines the following [=unloading document cleanup steps=] given a {{Document}} |document|:

1. If |document|'s [=salvageable=] state is true, then return.
1. Let |waiters| be a [=list/clone=] of |document|'s [=Document/registration waiters=].
1. [=set/Empty=] |document|'s [=Document/pending registrations=].
1. [=list/Empty=] |document|'s [=Document/registration buffer=] and [=Document/registration waiters=].
1. [=list/For each=] |waiter| of |waiters|:
  1. [=Reject=] |waiter|'s [=registration waiter/promise=] with an "{{AbortError}}" {{DOMException}}.

A subresource request already has a target window, so the browser queues the new attempt onto its document. During a navigation, the destination document does not exist yet, so attempts stay on the navigation request until HTML creates the document and attaches the same-origin ones.

<div algorithm="start a registration attempt">
  To <dfn export>start a registration attempt</dfn> given a [=/request=] |originating request| and a [=URL=] |registration URL|, with an optional [=URL=] <dfn export for="start a registration attempt">|provider URL|</dfn> and an optional [=string=] <dfn export for="start a registration attempt">|provider session ID|</dfn>:

  1. [=Assert=]: |originating request|'s [=request/current URL=]'s [=url/origin=] is [=same site=] with |registration URL|'s [=url/origin=].
  1. Let |attempt| be a new [=registration attempt=] whose [=registration attempt/registration URL=] is |registration URL|.
  1. If |provider URL| was given, then set |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/provider URL=] to |provider URL|.
  1. If |provider session ID| was given, then set |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/provider session ID=] to |provider session ID|.
  1. If |originating request| is a [=navigation request=]:
    1. [=list/Append=] |attempt| to |originating request|'s [=request/registration attempts=].
    1. Return |attempt|.
  1. Let |client| be |originating request|'s [=request/client=].
  1. If |client| is null or |client|'s [=environment settings object/global object=] is not a {{Window}}, then return |attempt|.
  1. If |client|'s [=environment settings object/origin=] is not [=same origin=] with |registration URL|'s [=url/origin=], then return |attempt|.
  1. Let |window| be |client|'s [=environment settings object/global object=].
  1. [=Queue a global task=] on the [=networking task source=] given |window| to run these steps:
    1. [=Attach a registration attempt=] given |window|'s [=associated Document=] and |attempt|.
  1. Return |attempt|.

  Note: [=HTTP-network fetch=] runs this step while processing response headers, so the task enters the [=networking task source=] before `fetch()` resolves. Multi-process implementations need to preserve that ordering across IPC.

  Note: If a Service Worker forwards a request with `respondWith(fetch(...))`, that `fetch()` creates a new [=/request=] whose [=request/client=] is the Service Worker, so the {{Document}} does not record registrations from its response.
</div>

<div algorithm>
  To <dfn>attach a registration attempt</dfn> given a {{Document}} |document| and a [=registration attempt=] |attempt|:

  1. If |document|'s [=Document/browsing context=] is null, then return.
  1. If |document|'s [=Document/origin=] is not [=same origin=] with |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/registration URL=]'s [=url/origin=], then return.
  1. Set |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/associated document=] to |document|.
  1. If |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/completed=] is true, then [=list/append=] |attempt| to |document|'s [=Document/registration buffer=].
  1. Otherwise, [=set/append=] |attempt| to |document|'s [=Document/pending registrations=].
</div>

<div algorithm>
  To <dfn export>attach navigation registration attempts</dfn> given a {{Document}} |document| and [=navigation params=] |navigationParams|:

  1. Let |request| be |navigationParams|'s [=navigation params/request=].
  1. If |request| is null, then return.
  1. [=list/For each=] |attempt| of |request|'s [=request/registration attempts=]:
    1. [=Attach a registration attempt=] given |document| and |attempt|.
</div>

When a registration finishes, the browser records its outcome and queues a task on the associated document to buffer the attempt and settle any waiting callers.

<div algorithm="complete a registration attempt">
  To <dfn export>complete a registration attempt</dfn> given a [=registration attempt=] |attempt| and a [=boolean=] |success|, with an optional [=device bound session=] <dfn export for="complete a registration attempt">|resulting session|</dfn>, an optional [=string=] <dfn export for="complete a registration attempt">|reason|</dfn>, and an optional [=16-bit unsigned integer=] <dfn export for="complete a registration attempt">|code|</dfn>:

  1. Set |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/end time=] to the [=current coarsened wall time=].
  1. Set |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/success=] to |success|.
  1. If |resulting session| was given, then set |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/resulting session=] to |resulting session|.
  1. If |reason| was given, then set |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/reason=] to |reason|.
  1. If |code| was given, then set |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/code=] to |code|.
  1. Set |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/completed=] to true.
  1. Let |document| be |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/associated document=].
  1. If |document| is null, then return.
  1. [=Queue a global task=] on the [=networking task source=] given |document|'s [=relevant global object=] to [=finalize a registration attempt=] given |document| and |attempt|.

  Note: This algorithm runs [=in parallel=] while attachment runs on the {{Document}} event loop. Multi-threaded implementations need synchronization around [=registration attempt/associated document=] and [=registration attempt/completed=] so an attempt finishing during handoff still moves into [=Document/registration buffer=].
</div>

<div algorithm>
  To <dfn>finalize a registration attempt</dfn> given a {{Document}} |document| and a [=registration attempt=] |attempt|:

  1. If |document|'s [=Document/pending registrations=] [=set/contains=] |attempt|:
    1. [=set/Remove=] |attempt| from |document|'s [=Document/pending registrations=].
    1. [=list/Append=] |attempt| to |document|'s [=Document/registration buffer=].
  1. [=Settle registration waiters=] given |document| and |attempt|.
</div>

<div algorithm>
  To <dfn>settle registration waiters</dfn> given a {{Document}} |document| and a [=registration attempt=] |attempt|:

  1. Let |waiters| be a [=list/clone=] of |document|'s [=Document/registration waiters=].
  1. [=list/For each=] |waiter| of |waiters|:
    1. If |waiter|'s [=registration waiter/remaining=] does not [=set/contain=] |attempt|, then [=iteration/continue=].
    1. [=set/Remove=] |attempt| from |waiter|'s [=registration waiter/remaining=].
    1. [=list/Append=] |attempt| to |waiter|'s [=registration waiter/captured attempts=].
    1. If |waiter|'s [=registration waiter/remaining=] is not [=set/is empty|empty=], then [=iteration/continue=].
    1. [=list/Remove=] |waiter| from |document|'s [=Document/registration waiters=].
    1. Let |results| be the result of [=collecting registration results=] given |waiter|'s [=registration waiter/captured attempts=] and |waiter|'s [=registration waiter/environment=].
    1. [=Resolve=] |waiter|'s [=registration waiter/promise=] with |results|.
</div>

# Extensions to the {{Navigator}} interface # {#navigator-extensions}

<pre class="idl">
partial interface Navigator {
  [SecureContext, SameObject] readonly attribute DeviceBoundSessionManager deviceBoundSessions;
};
</pre>

Each {{Navigator}} has an associated <dfn for="Navigator">device bound session manager</dfn> (null or a {{DeviceBoundSessionManager}}), initially null.

<div algorithm="Navigator.deviceBoundSessions">
  The <dfn attribute for="Navigator">deviceBoundSessions</dfn> getter steps are:

  1. If [=this=]'s [=Navigator/device bound session manager=] is null, then set [=this=]'s [=Navigator/device bound session manager=] to a [=new=] {{DeviceBoundSessionManager}} in [=this=]'s [=relevant realm=].
  1. Return [=this=]'s [=Navigator/device bound session manager=].
</div>

# The {{DeviceBoundSessionManager}} interface # {#device-bound-session-manager}

The <dfn interface>DeviceBoundSessionManager</dfn> interface lets scripts inspect active [=device bound sessions=] and wait for pending registrations on the current {{Document}}.

<pre class="idl">
[Exposed=Window, SecureContext]
interface DeviceBoundSessionManager {
  Promise&lt;sequence&lt;DeviceBoundSessionInfo>> getSessions();
  Promise&lt;sequence&lt;DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationResult>> waitForRegistrations(
    optional DeviceBoundSessionWaitOptions options = {}
  );
};

dictionary DeviceBoundSessionWaitOptions {
  AbortSignal signal;
};
</pre>

## {{DeviceBoundSessionManager/getSessions()}} method ## {#get-sessions-method}

`getSessions()` reads non-expired sessions from the session store in the background and resolves with info dictionaries for the ones visible to the caller.

<div algorithm="DeviceBoundSessionManager.getSessions()">
  When <dfn method for="DeviceBoundSessionManager">getSessions()</dfn> is called:

  1. Let |global| be [=this=]'s [=relevant global object=].
  1. If |global|'s [=associated Document=] is not [=Document/fully active=], then return [=a promise rejected with=] an "{{InvalidStateError}}" {{DOMException}} in [=this=]'s [=relevant realm=].
  1. Let |environment| be [=this=]'s [=relevant settings object=].
  1. Let |url| be |environment|'s [=environment/creation URL=].
  1. Let |promise| be [=a new promise=] in [=this=]'s [=relevant realm=].
  1. Run the following steps [=in parallel=]:
    1. Let |sessions| be the result of [=reading active sessions=] given |url|.
    1. [=Queue a global task=] on the [=networking task source=] given |global| to [=resolve=] |promise| with the result of [=collecting visible session infos=] given |sessions| and |environment|.
  1. Return |promise|.
</div>

<div algorithm>
  To <dfn>read active sessions</dfn> given a [=URL=] |url|:

  1. If |url|'s [=url/host=] is null, then return « ».
  1. Let |domain| be |url|'s [=url/host=]'s [=host/registrable domain=].
  1. If |domain| is null or [=session store=][|domain|] does not [=map/exist=], then return « ».
  1. Let |now| be the [=current coarsened wall time=].
  1. Let |sessions| be a new [=list=].
  1. [=list/For each=] |session| of [=session store=][|domain|]'s [=map/values=]:
    1. If |session|'s [=device bound session/expiration timestamp=] is not before |now|, then [=list/append=] |session| to |sessions|.
  1. Return |sessions|.
</div>

<div algorithm>
  To <dfn>collect visible session infos</dfn> given a [=list=] of [=device bound sessions=] |sessions| and an [=environment settings object=] |environment|:

  1. Let |results| be a new [=list=].
  1. [=list/For each=] |session| of |sessions|:
    1. If [=determine session visibility=] given |environment| and |session| is "`visible`", then [=list/append=] the result of [=creating a session info=] given |session| to |results|.
  1. Return |results|.
</div>

## {{DeviceBoundSessionManager/waitForRegistrations()}} method ## {#wait-for-registrations-method}

`waitForRegistrations()` waits for any registrations currently in flight on the document and resolves with the buffered outcomes sorted by completion time. When no registrations are in flight, it resolves right away. It ignores registrations started after the call.

A <dfn dictionary>DeviceBoundSessionWaitOptions</dfn> dictionary configures {{DeviceBoundSessionManager/waitForRegistrations()}}:

<dl dfn-for="DeviceBoundSessionWaitOptions">
  : <dfn dict-member>signal</dfn>
  :: An {{AbortSignal}} to abort the wait.
</dl>

<div algorithm="DeviceBoundSessionManager.waitForRegistrations()">
  When <dfn method for="DeviceBoundSessionManager">waitForRegistrations(|options|)</dfn> is called:

  1. Let |global| be [=this=]'s [=relevant global object=].
  1. Let |document| be |global|'s [=associated Document=].
  1. If |document| is not [=Document/fully active=], then return [=a promise rejected with=] an "{{InvalidStateError}}" {{DOMException}} in [=this=]'s [=relevant realm=].
  1. Let |signal| be |options|[{{DeviceBoundSessionWaitOptions/signal}}] [=map/with default=] null.
  1. If |signal| is non-null and |signal| is [=AbortSignal/aborted=], then return [=a promise rejected with=] |signal|'s [=AbortSignal/abort reason=] in [=this=]'s [=relevant realm=].
  1. Let |environment| be [=this=]'s [=relevant settings object=].
  1. If |document|'s [=Document/pending registrations=] [=set/is empty|is empty=]:
    1. Let |results| be the result of [=collecting registration results=] given |document|'s [=Document/registration buffer=] and |environment|.
    1. Return [=a promise resolved with=] |results| in [=this=]'s [=relevant realm=].
  1. Let |promise| be [=a new promise=] in [=this=]'s [=relevant realm=].
  1. Let |waiter| be a new [=registration waiter=] with:
      : [=registration waiter/promise=]
      :: |promise|
      : [=registration waiter/environment=]
      :: |environment|
      : [=registration waiter/remaining=]
      :: A [=set/clone=] of |document|'s [=Document/pending registrations=]
      : [=registration waiter/captured attempts=]
      :: A [=list/clone=] of |document|'s [=Document/registration buffer=]
  1. [=list/Append=] |waiter| to |document|'s [=Document/registration waiters=].
  1. If |signal| is non-null, then [=AbortSignal/add|add the following abort steps=] to |signal|:
    1. If |document|'s [=Document/registration waiters=] does not [=list/contain=] |waiter|, then return.
    1. [=list/Remove=] |waiter| from |document|'s [=Document/registration waiters=].
    1. [=Reject=] |promise| with |signal|'s [=AbortSignal/abort reason=].
  1. Return |promise|.
</div>

<div algorithm>
  To <dfn>collect registration results</dfn> given a [=list=] of completed [=registration attempts=] |attempts| and an [=environment settings object=] |environment|:

  1. Let |sorted attempts| be the result of [=list/sorting in ascending order=] |attempts|, with |a| being less than |b| if |a|'s [=registration attempt/end time=] is before |b|'s [=registration attempt/end time=].
  1. Let |results| be a new [=list=].
  1. [=list/For each=] |attempt| of |sorted attempts|:
    1. [=list/Append=] the result of [=creating a registration result=] given |attempt| and |environment| to |results|.
  1. Return |results|.
</div>

## Result dictionaries ## {#result-dictionaries}

<pre class="idl">
dictionary DeviceBoundSessionInfo {
  required DOMString sessionId;
  required USVString refreshUrl;
  required EpochTimeStamp creationTime;
};

dictionary DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationResult {
  required USVString registrationUrl;
  required EpochTimeStamp endTime;
  required boolean success;
  DeviceBoundSessionInfo session;
  DOMString reason;
  unsigned short code;
  USVString providerUrl;
  DOMString providerSessionId;
};
</pre>

### {{DeviceBoundSessionInfo}} dictionary ### {#session-info-dictionary}

A <dfn dictionary>DeviceBoundSessionInfo</dfn> dictionary describes an active [=device bound session=].

<dl dfn-for="DeviceBoundSessionInfo">
  : <dfn dict-member>sessionId</dfn>
  :: The session's [=device bound session/session identifier=].
  : <dfn dict-member>refreshUrl</dfn>
  :: The session's [=URL serializer|serialized=] [=device bound session/refresh URL=].
  : <dfn dict-member>creationTime</dfn>
  :: The number of milliseconds in the [=duration from=] the [=Unix epoch=] to the session's [=device bound session/creation time=], rounded down to the nearest integer.
</dl>

<div algorithm>
  To <dfn>create a session info</dfn> given a [=device bound session=] |session|:

  1. Let |info| be a new {{DeviceBoundSessionInfo}} dictionary with:
      : {{DeviceBoundSessionInfo/sessionId}}
      :: |session|'s [=device bound session/session identifier=].
      : {{DeviceBoundSessionInfo/refreshUrl}}
      :: The [=URL serializer=] of |session|'s [=device bound session/refresh URL=].
      : {{DeviceBoundSessionInfo/creationTime}}
      :: The number of milliseconds in the [=duration from=] the [=Unix epoch=] to |session|'s [=device bound session/creation time=], rounded down to the nearest integer.
  1. Return |info|.
</div>

### {{DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationResult}} dictionary ### {#registration-result-dictionary}

A <dfn dictionary>DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationResult</dfn> dictionary describes the outcome of a registration started by [=process a session registration=].

<dl dfn-for="DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationResult">
  : <dfn dict-member>registrationUrl</dfn>
  :: The [=URL serializer|serialized=] registration endpoint [=URL=].
  : <dfn dict-member>endTime</dfn>
  :: The number of milliseconds in the [=duration from=] the [=Unix epoch=] to the [=current coarsened wall time|coarsened wall time=] when the registration finished, rounded down to the nearest integer.

    Note: Because {{EpochTimeStamp}} uses the [=wall clock=], system clock adjustments can change the apparent order of results.
  : <dfn dict-member>success</dfn>
  :: True if the registration established a [=device bound session=], and false otherwise.
  : <dfn dict-member>session</dfn>
  :: The {{DeviceBoundSessionInfo}} for the newly created [=device bound session=], present when {{DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationResult/success}} is true and [=determine session visibility=] returns "`visible`" for the caller.

    Note: When `https://login.example.com` registers sessions scoped only to `https://app.example.com`, those sessions are not visible to `https://login.example.com`, so it receives the registration outcomes without {{DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationResult/session}}.
  : <dfn dict-member>reason</dfn>
  :: A coarse description of why registration failed, present when {{DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationResult/success}} is false.

    Issue: Replace the free-form string with a WebIDL enum of standardized failure reasons.
  : <dfn dict-member>code</dfn>
  :: The HTTP [=response/status=] code from the registration endpoint, present when registration failed due to that status.
  : <dfn dict-member>providerUrl</dfn>
  :: For a [[dbsc-1#federated-sessions|federated session]] registration, the [=URL serializer|serialized=] provider [=URL=] from the [:Secure-Session-Registration:] header.
  : <dfn dict-member>providerSessionId</dfn>
  :: For a [[dbsc-1#federated-sessions|federated session]] registration, the provider session identifier from the [:Secure-Session-Registration:] header.
</dl>

<div algorithm>
  To <dfn>create a registration result</dfn> given a [=registration attempt=] |attempt| and an [=environment settings object=] |environment|:

  1. [=Assert=]: |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/completed=] is true and |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/end time=] is non-null.
  1. Let |result| be a new {{DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationResult}} dictionary with:
      : {{DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationResult/registrationUrl}}
      :: The [=URL serializer=] of |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/registration URL=].
      : {{DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationResult/endTime}}
      :: The number of milliseconds in the [=duration from=] the [=Unix epoch=] to |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/end time=], rounded down to the nearest integer.
      : {{DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationResult/success}}
      :: |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/success=].
  1. Let |session| be |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/resulting session=].
  1. If |session| is non-null and [=determine session visibility=] given |environment| and |session| is "`visible`", then [=map/set=] |result|[{{DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationResult/session}}] to the result of [=creating a session info=] given |session|.
  1. If |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/reason=] is non-null, then [=map/set=] |result|[{{DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationResult/reason}}] to |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/reason=].
  1. If |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/code=] is non-null, then [=map/set=] |result|[{{DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationResult/code}}] to |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/code=].
  1. If |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/provider URL=] is non-null, then [=map/set=] |result|[{{DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationResult/providerUrl}}] to the [=URL serializer=] of |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/provider URL=].
  1. If |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/provider session ID=] is non-null, then [=map/set=] |result|[{{DeviceBoundSessionRegistrationResult/providerSessionId}}] to |attempt|'s [=registration attempt/provider session ID=].
  1. Return |result|.
</div>

# Session visibility # {#session-visibility}

A script can observe an active session (through `getSessions()` or a registration result's `session` field) only when its environment has storage access and its creation URL is in scope of the session (or matches the session's refresh URL).

<div algorithm>
  To <dfn export>determine session visibility</dfn> given an [=environment settings object=] |environment| and a [=device bound session=] |session|:

  1. If |environment| does not [=environment/has storage access|have storage access=], then return "`hidden`".
  1. Let |url| be |environment|'s [=environment/creation URL=].
  1. If |url| [=url/equals=] |session|'s [=device bound session/refresh URL=] with [=url/equals/exclude fragments=] set to true, then return "`visible`".
  1. If the result of running [=algorithms/determine if a URL is in scope=] with |url| and |session| is "`include`", then return "`visible`".
  1. Return "`hidden`".
</div>

<!-- This is an alternative to checking for [=environment/has storage access=] above.

<div algorithm>
To <dfn>check whether credentials would be included</dfn>, given an [=environment settings object=] |environment| and a [=device bound session=] |session|:

  1. Let |url| be |environment|'s [=environment/creation URL=].
    Note: |url| can be reused from an earlier step if merged into the visibility algo.
  1. Let |request| be a new [=request=] whose [=request/URL=] is |url|, [=request/method=] is \``GET`\`, [=request/client=] is |environment|, [=request/mode=] is "`same-origin`", and [=request/credentials mode=] is "`include`".
  1. [=list/For each=] |credential| of |session|'s [=device bound session/session credentials=]:
    1. If |credential|'s [=session credential/type=] is "`cookie`", and a cookie with |credential|'s [=session credential/attributes=] would be attached to |request| (see [[RFC6265#cookie]]), then return "visible".
  1. Return "hidden".
</div>

-->

<div class="example" id="session-visibility-example">

  Issue: Consider making this a WPT instead.

  Given the following (incomplete) session definition:

  ```js
  {
    "session_identifier": "session_id",
    "refresh_url": "/refresh",
    "scope": {
      "origin": "https://example.com",
      "include_site": true,
      "scope_specification" : [
        { "type": "exclude", "domain": "sites.example.com", "path": "/" },
        { "type": "exclude", "domain": "*.example.com", "path": "/static" }
      ]
    },
    "credentials": [{
      "type": "cookie",
      "name": "auth_cookie",
      "attributes": "Domain=example.com; Path=/; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Strict"
    }]
  }
  ```

  This table shows where `session_id` is visible:

  <table>
    <tr>
        <th>Creation URL</th>
        <th>Storage access</th>
        <th>Visible?</th>
        <th>Reason</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://example.com/account`</td>
        <td>Top-level window</td>
        <td>`true`</td>
        <td>In scope of `session_id`, has storage access.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://sub.example.com/app`</td>
        <td>Top-level window</td>
        <td>`true`</td>
        <td>Also in scope of `session_id`, by its `include_site`.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://example.com/refresh`</td>
        <td>Top-level window</td>
        <td>`true`</td>
        <td>Refresh URL bypasses scope check.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://example.com/refresh`</td>
        <td>Embedded without storage access</td>
        <td>`false`</td>
        <td>No access to 1P `example.com` storage.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://sites.example.com/a`</td>
        <td>N/A</td>
        <td>`false`</td>
        <td>URL matches the `sites.example.com/` exclusion rule.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><code>https://app.example.com/<wbr>static/index.html</code></td>
        <td>N/A</td>
        <td>`false`</td>
        <td>URL matches the `*.example.com/static` exclusion rule.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

</div>

# Changes to other specifications # {#changes-to-other-specifications}

DBSC starts and completes registration attempts during background network processing, while Fetch and HTML carry navigation-triggered attempts onto the resulting document.

## Changes to the Fetch specification ## {#changes-to-fetch}

A [=/request=] has an associated <dfn for="request">registration attempts</dfn>, a [=list=] of [=registration attempts=], initially empty.

In [=HTTP-network-or-cache fetch=], after setting *httpRequest* to a [=request/clone=] of *request*, set *httpRequest*'s [=request/registration attempts=] to *request*'s [=request/registration attempts=] (sharing the same [=list=]).

Note: Sharing [=request/registration attempts=] with *httpRequest* keeps [=registration attempts=] started on per-hop network requests (including redirects) on the originating navigation [=/request=] in [=navigation params=].

## Changes to the HTML specification ## {#changes-to-html}

In [=create and initialize a Document object=], after initializing the {{Document}} *document* from *navigationParams*, run [=attach navigation registration attempts=] given *document* and *navigationParams*.

## Changes to the DBSC specification ## {#changes-to-dbsc}

Issue: Avoid deep monkey-patching here: open a PR against [[dbsc-1]], then remove this section.

In [=device bound session=]:

- Change [=device bound session/refresh URL=]'s type from a [=string=] to a [=URL=].
- Specify that [=device bound session/expiration timestamp=] is a moment on the [=wall clock=].
- Add the following [=struct/item=]:
    : <dfn for="device bound session">creation time</dfn>
    :: A [=coarsened moment=] on the [=wall clock=], set to the [=current coarsened wall time=] when this session was created.

In [=process a session registration=], for each valid entry in *registration list* after resolving *endpoint* to a [=URL=] (ignoring entries where URL parsing fails):

1. If *response*'s [=response/URL=] is null or *response*'s [=response/URL=]'s [=url/origin=] is not [=same site=] with *endpoint*'s [=url/origin=], then [=iteration/continue=].
1. Let *attempt* be [=start a registration attempt|the result of starting a registration attempt=] given *request* and *endpoint*, with:
  - [=start a registration attempt/provider URL=] set to *provider URL* if *params*["`provider_url`"] exists, is an `sf-string`, and running the [=URL parser=] on *params*["`provider_url`"] returns a [=URL=] *provider URL*, and
  - [=start a registration attempt/provider session ID=] set to *params*["`provider_session_id`"] if *params*["`provider_session_id`"] exists and is an `sf-string`.
1. Run the remaining steps for the entry [=in parallel=]:
  1. If *key pair* is "`failure`", then [=complete a registration attempt=] given *attempt* and false, with [=complete a registration attempt/reason=] set to an appropriate failure reason, and abort these steps.
  1. Pass *attempt* as an additional optional input to [=algorithms/send a request=].

Note: Only new session registrations (*session id* is null) pass *attempt* to the next two algorithms. Session refreshes omit it.

In [=algorithms/send a request=]:

1. Accept an optional [=registration attempt=] *attempt*.
1. Check *originating request*'s [=request/current URL=]'s [=url/origin=] (instead of *originating request*'s [=request/URL=]'s [=url/origin=]) when verifying that the request is [=same site=] with *destination*'s [=url/origin=].
1. Whenever *attempt* was given and the algorithm skips the request or returns early due to validation failure, a [=network error=], or an HTTP [=response/status=] code, [=complete a registration attempt=] given *attempt* and false, with [=complete a registration attempt/reason=] set to an appropriate failure reason (and [=complete a registration attempt/code=] set to *response*'s [=response/status=] when a [=response=] was received).
1. Pass *attempt* (if given) to [=create a session=].

In [=create a session=]:

1. Accept an optional [=registration attempt=] *attempt*.
1. After setting the [=device bound session/expiration timestamp=]:
  1. If *session id* is non-null, [=session store=][*destination domain*] [=map/exists=], and [=session store=][*destination domain*][*session id*] [=map/exists=], then set *session*'s [=device bound session/creation time=] to [=session store=][*destination domain*][*session id*]'s [=device bound session/creation time=].
  1. Otherwise, set *session*'s [=device bound session/creation time=] to the [=current coarsened wall time=].
1. If *attempt* was given:
  1. After adding *session* to the [=session store=] and caching any challenge from *response*, [=complete a registration attempt=] given *attempt* and true, with [=complete a registration attempt/resulting session=] set to *session*.
  1. If the algorithm returns without adding *session* to the [=session store=] (including when terminating an existing session or when *response* sets none of *session*'s [=device bound session/session credentials=]), [=complete a registration attempt=] given *attempt* and false, with [=complete a registration attempt/reason=] set to an appropriate failure reason.
